# GuiState / async-worker test preconditions (regression prevention)

Two failure classes found in practice (`SearchControllerTests` stack-use-after-scope
and UIThreadOwned assert aborts). When writing or modifying tests:

## 1. Mark the test thread as the UI thread

Tests that touch `GuiState` (even indirectly, through `SearchController::Update`, the
results table helpers, etc.) must run on a thread registered with `MarkCurrentThreadAsUI()`.
`UIThreadOwned<T>` mutable accessors assert `IsUIThread()` in debug builds and will abort
otherwise. Use the custom-`main` pattern (`tests/GuiStateTests.cpp:31-36`):

```cpp
#define DOCTEST_CONFIG_IMPLEMENT  // NOT IMPLEMENT_WITH_MAIN when you define main()
#include "doctest/doctest.h"

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  MarkCurrentThreadAsUI();
  doctest::Context context(argc, argv);
  return context.run();
}
```

## 2. Quiesce async workers before scope teardown

Never end a test body while `SearchWorker::IsBusy()` is true — the worker captures
stack references (`AppSettings const*`, `FileIndex&`) in its search params and will
produce an ASan stack-use-after-scope when the test scope unwinds. Before the test
function returns, disarm the trigger and drain:

```cpp
state.autoRefresh = false;  // or whatever trigger was armed
while (search_worker->IsBusy()) {
  std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(2));
}
```

## 3. Prefer tests that register invariants over deep polling loops

When adding a regression test for a crash, keep it minimal and anchored to the
specific invariant (see `.cursor/rules/imgui-test-engine-preconditions.mdc` for
Test Engine–driven tests).

**References:** `tests/GuiStateTests.cpp` (main pattern),
`tests/SearchControllerTests.cpp` (`RepeatedAutoRefresh...` quiesce block),
`.cursor/rules/ui-state-write-confinement-cpp.mdc` (ownership),
`.cursor/rules/production-async-future-cpp.mdc` (future cleanup in tests too).
